<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 7 August, from 461 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">461 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,565 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Western Emperor Majorian is executed on Ricimer's orders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Majorian, the last Western emperor to attempt a real recovery of the empire, was arrested and beheaded by his general Ricimer. Afterwards Ricimer ruled through puppet emperors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1461">1461 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">565 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">General Cao Qin's rebellion against the Tianshun Emperor fails</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fearing a purge by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhengtong-emperor">Tianshun Emperor</a>, General Cao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> and his troops rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, set fire to gates of the Imperial City and killed several leading ministers. Cornered within a day, Cao was forced to take his own life.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhengtong-emperor">Zhengtong Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1479">1479 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">547 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maximilian of Habsburg defeats the French at Guinegate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor">Maximilian of Habsburg</a>, the future Emperor Maximilian I, defeated the French troops of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a>. It was the first battle in which the Swiss pike square was used by a power that was not natively Swiss.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor">Maximilian I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1744">1744 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">282 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prussia begins the Second Silesian War against Austria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fearing that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> would retake Silesia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> declared its intervention in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a> on behalf of Emperor Charles VII. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-silesian-war">Second Silesian War</a> ended in 1745 with the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a>, which confirmed Prussian possession of Silesia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-silesian-war">Second Silesian War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vii-holy-roman-emperor">Charles VII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1782">1782 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">244 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington creates the Badge of Military Merit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington established a purple cloth heart to honour enlisted soldiers for meritorious action. Revived in 1932 as the Purple Heart, it is now awarded to those wounded or killed in US service.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1819">1819 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">207 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simón Bolívar wins the Battle of Boyacá</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a daring march over the Andes, Bolívar's army defeated the royalists at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> fell days later, securing the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>, present-day Colombia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Marines land on Guadalcanal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US Marines landed on Guadalcanal in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands, the first major American offensive of the Pacific war. Six months of fighting ended in a Japanese withdrawal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thor Heyerdahl's Kon-Tiki raft reaches Polynesia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After 101 days and some 7,000 km from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thor">Thor</a> Heyerdahl's balsa raft ran onto the reef at Raroia. The voyage showed that prehistoric people could have crossed the Pacific on such craft.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1998">1998 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Al-Qaeda bombs US embassies in Kenya and Tanzania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Truck bombs exploded almost simultaneously at the US embassies in Nairobi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dar-es-salaam">Dar es Salaam</a>, killing 224 people, most of them Africans. The attacks brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osama-bin-laden">Osama bin Laden</a> to world attention.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 7 August <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-v-of-leon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-v-of-leon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso V of León</span><span class="tp">994–1028</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1050–1106</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vincenzo-scamozzi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vincenzo-scamozzi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vincenzo Scamozzi</span><span class="tp">1548–1616</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mariano-arista"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mariano-arista.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mariano Arista</span><span class="tp">1802–1855</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-stanislavski"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/konstantin-stanislavski.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Konstantin Stanislavski</span><span class="tp">1863–1938</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rabindranath-tagore"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rabindranath-tagore.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rabindranath Tagore</span><span class="tp">1861–1941</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
